<%# The prose here is English and lives in the template rather than in a locale
    file, because unlike every other screen this file has exactly one language —
    see CrawlersController#llms. Everything named below comes from `Landing`, so
    a card added to the landing page shows up here without a second edit. %>
# UTCC AI Academy

> <%= t("meta.description") %>

The site is Thai-first. A bare URL is Thai, and `?lang=en` on any of them is the
same page in English — the links below are the English ones. A browser sending
`Accept-Language` gets the language it asked for without the parameter.

Only the pages listed under Pages are readable without an account. The rest of the
site — the course catalog, the lessons, a learner's progress and the leaderboard —
is a private area for enrolled students and answers a redirect to the home page.

It is run by the <%= t("meta.org_name") %>.

## Pages

- [Home](<%= locale_url(:en, path: root_path) %>): what the academy is, the topics it covers, the learning tracks, projects from students, upcoming events, and a FAQ.
- [Privacy notice](<%= locale_url(:en, path: privacy_path) %>): what student data is collected and why, under Thailand's PDPA.
- [Terms of use](<%= locale_url(:en, path: terms_path) %>): the terms a student accepts when signing up.

